        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="0473" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg365"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Durham to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Fort au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received January 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 142.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Continuing my dispatch of this morning, I
                    beg leave to say that several attempts have been made by the Haitian authorities
                    to have me depart from your verbal instruction to have no written correspondence
                    on the subject of the Mevs case. To-day I received a memorandum from the
                    minister of foreign relations in which several of my statements are distorted,
                    obviously with a view to opening a controversy. I inclose a copy of the
                    memorandum with translation, together with my reply, declining to write
                    concerning the matter at that stage.</p>
                <p>I shall continue to insist that some statement be made on the point of lack of
                    courtesy.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John S. Durham.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d356-a1.xml" xpointer="d356-a1"/>
